{"resourceIdentifier":"3745","resourceName":"Enexor Impact USA","description":"The Enexor Impact USA Project is a grouped project that generates emissions reductions through the deployment of Enexor’s Bio-CHP™ systems at client facilities across the United States. These modular, on-site systems convert organic and non-recyclable plastic waste into renewable electricity and thermal energy. Leveraging Enexor’s proprietary Bio-CHP™ technology, the project simultaneously addresses two major emissions sources: fossil fuel-based energy generation and landfill methane emissions. System performance and emissions reductions are continuously monitored through remote data systems and a secure cloud-based platform, ensuring accurate tracking and verification. Overall, the project represents a distributed infrastructure model for decarbonization, transforming waste liabilities into energy assets while generating verifiable carbon credits at scale.","location":{"latitude":36.237327,"longitude":86.319558},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":{"startInclusive":"2023-05-03","endExclusive":"2023-06-03","endInclusive":"2023-06-02"},"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"3745"}]},{"code":"STATE_PROVINCE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"TN"}]}],"participationSummaries":[{"programCode":"VCS","attributes":[{"code":"PROPONENT_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Enexor BioEnergy"},{"type":"string","value":"TN, United States"},{"type":"string","value":"5169986482"},{"type":"string","value":"sagar@enexor.com"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_STATUS","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Registered"}]},{"code":"EST_ANNUAL_EMISSION_REDCT","values":[{"type":"string","value":"1016760"}]},{"code":"PRIMARY_PROJECT_CATEGORY_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Energy industries (renewable/non-renewable sources)"}]},{"code":"PROTOCOL_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"VM0018,ACM0022"}]},{"code":"VALIDATOR_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","valu